WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.213
<v Narrator>One number for everything a city does: potholes,

2
00:00:06.293 --> 00:00:09.410
<v Narrator>trash, questions, and sometimes an emergency.

3
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.403
<v Narrator>A phone tree makes residents pick a branch, and a language.

4
00:00:13.483 --> 00:00:15.430
<v Narrator>This assistant just listens.

5
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:26.020
<v Narrator>Residents call a Teams phone number, through Teams Phone extensibility.

6
00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:31.257
<v Narrator>Azure Communication Services Call Automation bridges the audio to Voice Live,

7
00:00:31.337 --> 00:00:34.200
<v Narrator>where GPT Realtime holds the conversation.

8
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:39.260
<v Narrator>The city's server decides, and hands off to a Teams call queue with context.

9
00:00:41.683 --> 00:00:46.133
<v Narrator>First, Alex Chen reports a pothole the way people actually talk.

10
00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:50.866
<v Agent>City of Contoso 311. I'm an automated assistant.

11
00:00:50.946 --> 00:00:55.135
<v Agent>For emergencies, hang up and dial 911. How can I help?

12
00:00:55.215 --> 00:00:57.900
<v Agent>Para español, hable en español.

13
00:00:59.211 --> 00:01:04.141
<v Alex>Hi, there's a big pothole on Oak Avenue, right at the corner of Fifth Street.

14
00:01:04.505 --> 00:01:08.325
<v Agent>I have the pothole at Oak Avenue and 5th Street. Is that right?

15
00:01:09.666 --> 00:01:13.944
<v Narrator>The server, not the model, found that corner on the city's map.

16
00:01:14.024 --> 00:01:16.786
<v Narrator>Nothing is filed until Alex confirms.

17
00:01:17.653 --> 00:01:19.033
<v Alex>Yes, that's right.

18
00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:27.198
<v Agent>I've filed a pothole report at Oak Avenue and 5th Street with Public Works.

19
00:01:27.278 --> 00:01:34.139
<v Agent>Your case number is S R, 2 6, 0 1 9 3. Again, S R, 2 6, 0 1 9 3.

20
00:01:34.483 --> 00:01:38.083
<v Agent>Would you like text updates on this case, or is there anything else?

21
00:01:39.425 --> 00:01:42.235
<v Alex>Yes, text me updates please.

22
00:01:42.571 --> 00:01:45.962
<v Agent>Done. I've texted your case number to the number you're calling from.

23
00:01:46.042 --> 00:01:48.341
<v Agent>Is there anything else I can help you with?

24
00:01:49.664 --> 00:01:52.025
<v Narrator>A text goes out only with consent.

25
00:01:52.105 --> 00:01:54.604
<v Narrator>The model never sees Alex's number.

26
00:01:55.469 --> 00:01:58.089
<v Alex>No, that's all, thanks.

27
00:01:58.425 --> 00:02:02.405
<v Agent>Thank you for calling City of Contoso 311. Goodbye.

28
00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:07.466
<v Narrator>Some calls must never become a service request.

29
00:02:07.546 --> 00:02:11.250
<v Narrator>Sam Rivera smells gas in his kitchen, and he's called 311.

30
00:02:12.201 --> 00:02:16.421
<v Sam>Hi, I smell gas in my kitchen and I'm not sure what to do.

31
00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:19.313
<v Agent>This sounds like a gas emergency.

32
00:02:19.393 --> 00:02:24.119
<v Agent>Please leave the building now and don't switch anything on or off.

33
00:02:24.199 --> 00:02:29.070
<v Agent>Once you're outside, call the gas utility at 555-0109, or dial 911.

34
00:02:30.414 --> 00:02:33.650
<v Narrator>That was the server's rule, not the model's judgment.

35
00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:37.264
<v Narrator>It checks every caller turn first: no questions, no case.

36
00:02:39.302 --> 00:02:42.742
<v Narrator>Lucía Ortega calls the same number, in Spanish.

37
00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:47.446
<v Agent>City of Contoso 311. I'm an automated assistant.

38
00:02:47.526 --> 00:02:51.715
<v Agent>For emergencies, hang up and dial 911. How can I help?

39
00:02:51.795 --> 00:02:54.480
<v Agent>Para español, hable en español.

40
00:02:55.783 --> 00:02:59.813
<v Lucía>Hola, necesito que recojan un colchón y un sofá viejo.

41
00:03:00.128 --> 00:03:03.330
<v Agent>Puedo programar la recogida de un colchón y un sofá.

42
00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.708
<v Agent>¿Cuál es la dirección de recogida?

43
00:03:07.051 --> 00:03:08.293
<v Narrator>Nobody pressed 2.

44
00:03:08.373 --> 00:03:12.046
<v Narrator>The server heard Spanish and switched the same agent's language

45
00:03:12.126 --> 00:03:14.241
<v Narrator>and voice, under the same rules.

46
00:03:15.073 --> 00:03:17.553
<v Lucía>En el 1200 de Maple Street.

47
00:03:17.861 --> 00:03:26.783
<v Agent>La recogida está programada para el sábado 3 de octubre en 1200 Maple Street.

48
00:03:26.863 --> 00:03:31.760
<v Agent>Su número de caso es S R, 2 6, 0 1 9 4.

49
00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:35.441
<v Agent>Repito, S R, 2 6, 0 1 9 4.

50
00:03:35.786 --> 00:03:39.656
<v Agent>¿Quiere recibir actualizaciones por mensaje de texto sobre este caso,

51
00:03:39.736 --> 00:03:40.916
<v Agent>o hay algo más?

52
00:03:43.396 --> 00:03:45.536
<v Narrator>Later, Sam calls back with questions.

53
00:03:45.616 --> 00:03:49.316
<v Narrator>The model may answer them only from articles the city has approved.

54
00:03:50.251 --> 00:03:52.571
<v Sam>And what are the counter hours at City Hall?

55
00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.981
<v Agent>I don't have approved information on that, so I won't guess.

56
00:03:56.061 --> 00:03:58.680
<v Agent>Would you like me to connect you with 311 staff?

57
00:04:00.057 --> 00:04:03.877
<v Narrator>The only match was an expired notice, so the server withheld it.

58
00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:06.100
<v Sam>No, that's all.

59
00:04:06.403 --> 00:04:10.383
<v Agent>Thank you for calling City of Contoso 311. Goodbye.

60
00:04:12.433 --> 00:04:13.899
<v Narrator>Next, a complaint.

61
00:04:13.979 --> 00:04:16.514
<v Narrator>The server's policy is to apologize,

62
00:04:16.594 --> 00:04:19.923
<v Narrator>promise nothing, and offer a report or a person.

63
00:04:20.921 --> 00:04:22.648
<v Resident>I want to make a complaint.

64
00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:26.159
<v Resident>The trash trucks have skipped my street three weeks in a row

65
00:04:26.239 --> 00:04:28.201
<v Resident>and nobody has called me back.

66
00:04:28.515 --> 00:04:31.619
<v Agent>I'm sorry about that. I can hear how frustrating it is.

67
00:04:31.699 --> 00:04:33.945
<v Agent>I can file a missed-pickup report now,

68
00:04:34.025 --> 00:04:38.675
<v Agent>or connect you with a 311 staff member who can look into it. Which would you prefer?

69
00:04:39.997 --> 00:04:42.587
<v Resident>I'd like to talk to a person, please.

70
00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.580
<v Agent>I'm connecting you with 311 staff now.

71
00:04:46.956 --> 00:04:50.291
<v Narrator>The server checked the hours and picked the Teams queue.

72
00:04:50.371 --> 00:04:53.626
<v Narrator>Staff see the topic, a summary and the caller's mood.

73
00:04:56.083 --> 00:04:57.735
<v Narrator>Five calls, one number.

74
00:04:57.815 --> 00:05:00.027
<v Narrator>The model held each conversation;

75
00:05:00.107 --> 00:05:03.683
<v Narrator>the city's server decided every outcome, and audited it.

76
00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.962
<v Narrator>The model converses and calls tools.

77
00:05:08.042 --> 00:05:11.760
<v Narrator>Every line the caller hears is written by the server.

78
00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.678
<v Narrator>The server checks the place, the rules

79
00:05:14.758 --> 00:05:17.970
<v Narrator>and the hours before it files, texts or transfers.

80
00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:23.445
<v Narrator>Making it yours is mostly configuration: request rules,

81
00:05:23.525 --> 00:05:27.360
<v Narrator>departments and hours, emergency phrases, and approved articles.

82
00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:32.450
<v Narrator>The spec and this demo script give your coding agent the context for the rest.

83
00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.597
<v Narrator>311 Service Assistant.

84
00:05:36.677 --> 00:05:40.690
<v Narrator>Run it in simulation, then connect it to your city's Teams number.
